 high capacity well  for water access and you can irrigate if  you have a golf course for example  if you're building a car wash you can  get a high capacity well but if you  want to irrigate crops grow  food you can't greg donald with the pei  potato board agrees and says the  moratorium on agricultural irrigation  needs to be suspended  we're getting hotter higher temperatures  longer periods without rain  wind and it irrigation is another tool  that we need in addition to those  in nova scotia dry hot conditions are  making for a tough summer for many  farmers but there is one crop that's  thriving  grapes need about half the water than a  norm a lot of other crops need  so we're doing great it's looking like  it could be a great finish this year  there is one big challenge this year  though covet 19 has created a labor  shortage at vineyards across the region  come harvest time l's will be short for  temporary foreign workers  we have made it up with local workers  and they're doing a great job but we're  still just missing those experienced  professional hands  the pei federation of agriculture say  they met with premier dennis king last  week  and will meet again this week to examine  irrigation opportunities  in the meantime they'll hold out hope  for rain jesse thomas global news  sheffield mills nova scotia  still ahead why pandemic restrictions  are turning european travelers  topsy turvy  welcome back this summer most canadians  opted to vacation  at home or travel within the country but  canada  is very big of course similar in size to  all of europe which is home to more than  50 countries  and europeans are now struggling to  navigate a constantly changing landscape  of travel  restrictions redmond shannon reports  from london  [Music]  in normal times europe is a dream for  travellers  open borders cheap flights and fast  trains  but ever since the start of the covet 19  pandemic  the rules have changed in fact they've  never stopped changing  countries across europe are imposing  sudden mandatory self-isolation rules on  people traveling from  virus hotspots often with little notice  yeah rather rather be here in time than  have to quarantine for two weeks  on thursday germany asked its citizens  to stop traveling to at-risk  countries but what if you're already on  holiday  a lot can change during a two-week  vacation we asked before we  before we camped and it was a green zone  but no  it's a risk zone even britain's  transport secretary was forced to  isolate when the rules changed during  his vacation to spain  travelers are keeping a close eye on  this covid 19  case map yellow regions are generally  safe to return from  but coming from a brown area means you  might have to self-isolate  but each country has a different  threshold and the sudden rule changes  have caused  diplomatic tension we appeal to uk  government to replace this 14 days  quarantine measured by reliable tests  with so many people wary of travel  tourist meccas like venice  are almost empty we went into the doge's  palace  and we went into one of the main museums  to see a tintoretto  and i kid you not there must have been  12 people  instead of a thousand when i put my just  my tourist hat on it was amazing you  know it was like such a  wonderful experience just walking around  the city without massive crowds  but it's been devastating for the  tourism industry and for the foreseeable  future traveling abroad will be a role  of the dice  to say that this is frustrating and  confusing is to put it mildly  but if i was to be generous to the  health officials i would say is that  well i don't know what else  they can do having those rules is one  thing  abiding by them is another the eu's  trade commissioner was forced to resign  this week  after failing to self-isolate on a trip  home to ireland  redmond shannon global news london  up next why this canadian collection of  superhero stories  just received super rare status  [Music]  welco